  iadas:authorConclusion "The current findings support body talk and fat talk as a potential risk factor for eating disorders among male. Muscle-focused body talk may not a risk factor for diagnostic eating disorder symptoms. Muscle talk among male is related less to muscle dissatisfaction and more to male socioalization processes. Athletic identity did non emerge as a significant moderator of the association between body talk and eating disorder symptoms. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_108>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_108>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Mixed%20sport>;
  iadas:limites "The study was limited to a single university campus in the southeastern United States, limiting generalizability of the findings. Few participants endorsed aesthetic or lean sports, potentially attenuating results. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """Future work may benefit from using a more objective of body composition. 
Future work should explore such associations among male in a clinical sample, examining whether fat or muscle talk is associated with eating disorder and/or muscle dysmorphia symptom severity. 
Fat talk may be an important prevention target amon male, regardless of athletic identity. """;
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.23 , p<,01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "224";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1080> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "1080";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Perceptions of mastery climate, autonomy-support, and performance climate at preseason predicted higher self esteem and lower disordered eating during competitive season, through mediation of perceived competence. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1080>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1080>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/gymnastics>;
  iadas:limites "We included a purposeful sample of competitive gymnasts, so our results may not generalize to other youth sport contexts. It should be noted that after removing unreliable items, performance climate in our study only tapped the unequal recognition aspect. Participants reported low lecels of performance climate. We could not examine the effect of controlling behaviors because this construct showed a poor fit in the model. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives "More theory driven longitudinal studies can determine relationships and mediation over time and inform interventions to promote well-being among youth partcicipants. Future research should continue to consider indices of physical, social, emotional, and cognitive maturity with youth samples to control for developmental differences in well-being outcomes. ";
