  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1098>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Athletics>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ashtanga%20yoga>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/circus>;
  iadas:limites "The results of the present study were based on online data gathering which questions the representative nature of the sample. Although participants were represented in a broad range of age and educational level, the highest proportion of participants were young and highly qualified Female. The participation in the research was voluntary thus the increased interest towards the topic of the examination might bias the results. The correlational desing of the present study does not allow causal inferences. The subject of the present study was the tendency to orthorexia nercosa, not orthorexia nervosa as a diagnosis, the results cannot be fully transposed into orthorexia nervosa since no orthorexia diagnosed patients are available yet. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "A viable next step in orthorexia nervosa research could be the use of experience sampling method which could provide important information about the daily fluctuation of orthorexia nervosa and the related variables. It would be benefical to collect information about the type of the exercise as well, because some sport activities (category sports, aesthetic sport) can mean a higher vulnerability to orthorexia. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.48, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "739";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1099> a iadas:Analysis;
