<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_11> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "11";
  iadas:authorConclusion "This study supports a dual-pathway model of muscle dysmorphia, where sociocultural pressure influences symptoms both indirectly via appearance motivation and directly, with cognitive flexibility acting as a protective moderator. It highlights the interplay between social, motivational, and cognitive factors";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_11>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_11>;
  iadas:limites "The cross-sectional design limits causal interpretation, and the use of a convenience, all-male sample restricts generalizability. Additionally, the measure of sociocultural pressure was not specific to muscularity ideals";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research should use longitudinal designs and more diverse samples to validate the model. Interventions enhancing cognitive flexibility and promoting non-appearance-based exercise motives appear promising avenues for prevention and treatment.";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.550, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "95";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_110> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "110";
  iadas:authorConclusion "This study highlights a higher risk of orthorexia nervosa (OrNe) among male students, with strong associations with dieting behaviors and, in females, BMI. It emphasizes the multifactorial nature of OrNe and the importance of early identification in young athletes.";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_110>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_110>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Badminton>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/basketball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/football>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/other%20sport>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/weightlifting>;
  iadas:limites "The cross-sectional design limits causal inference, and self-reported measures may introduce bias. Additionally, mental health assessment tools and limited comparability with prior studies restrict interpretation.";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research should include longitudinal designs, more diverse populations, and more specific mental health measures. Preventive strategies targeting dietary behaviors and body-related factors in university and sports settings are needed.";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=-.041, p=.505";
