<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1395> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "1395";
  iadas:authorConclusion "This studies clarifies notable correlates, particularly overweight preoccupation, of eating pathology in male athletes and highlights sport confidence as a potential prevention and intervention target. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1395>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1395>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Cross%20country>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/baseball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/basketball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/diving>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/football>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/golf>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/lacrosse>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/soccer>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/tennis>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/track%20and%20field>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/wrestling>;
  iadas:limites "Causality cannot be inffered from cross sectional findings and the causality of risk factors for eating pathology in male athletes remains unclear. Internal consistency of the purging subscale of the EPSI was poor. Alternately, the items composing this subscale may not adequately reflect compensatory purging behaviors or its underlying motivations in this population. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research would benefit from a larger sample without preset body dissatisfaction criteria to ensure adequate power for moderation, to allow for direct comparison across sport types, positions, and competition levels, and to avoid potential floor effects. More longitudinal and mediational designs are needed to model how sport related pressures relate to these varied correlates. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.19, N.S.";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "93";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

