<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1456> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "1456";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Significant correlation were found between muscle dysmorphia and body dysmorphic disorder symptoms. The correlational data suggested a relationship between the symptoms of muscle dysmorphia and eating disorders. Small but significant correlations were found between the substance use subscale of the MASS and the laxatives, diuretics behavioral question of the EAT-26, between the injury risk subscale of the MASS and the vomit and exercise behavioral questions of the EAT-26, and between the muscle satisfaction subscale and the binge eating and the lost > 9kg behavioral questions of the EAT-26. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1456>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1456>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Weightlifting>;
  iadas:limites "The EAT-26 may not be sensitive to muscularity oriented disordered eating and body image concerns. The current research consisted of an online survey, therefore the possibility existed that participants might have interpreted the meanings of questions or statements differently to those intended or might have perceived some of the statements or questions as vague. Self selection bias is a limitation of internet surveys. The data were exclusively based on self report which can have tendencies toward social desirability bias. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives "A better understanding and awareness of the rates and symptoms of muscle dysmorphia and body dismorphic disorder and eating disorders may help strength and conditioning professionals to identify and refer at risk individuals for help from mental health professionals. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.411, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "648";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Power";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

