<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1514> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "1514";
  iadas:authorConclusion "The study highlights strong links between exercise addiction, muscle dysmorphia, and multiple addictions, with impulsivity playing a key mediating role. These findings emphasize the importance of targeting impulsivity and emotion regulation in prevention and treatment";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1514>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1514>;
  iadas:limites "The cross-sectional design prevents causal conclusions, and the use of a homogeneous convenience sample limits generalizability. Additionally, reliance on screening tools rather than clinical diagnoses may affect accuracy.";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research should use longitudinal designs to clarify causal relationships and further explore specific dimensions of impulsivity. There is also a need to develop prevention and intervention strategies focusing on emotion regulation and impulsivity";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.13, p<.05";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "315";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

