<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1850> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "1850";
  iadas:authorConclusion "We observed an overall, negative linear relationship between self regulatory eating attitudes and disordered eating in the sports contexts. The overall relationship between self regulatory eating attitudes and disordered eating was not totally linear. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1850>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1850>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Aesthetic>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/endurance>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/weight%20category>;
  iadas:limites "Data were self-reported and could biased by social desirability. Correlation analyses were used, which limits the generalization of the demonstrated relationshipw between variables. The ZOREAS could be compared to the individual zone of optimal functioning, and like the latter, could vary according to the sport and the indivdiual. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future longitudinal studies could determine the stability and the specificity of the ZOREAS, while an experimental study would help to etablish the direction of causality suggested by our correlation analysis. This type of research would help in developing educational programs based on self-regulation of eating attitude adaptation that seek to limit the emergence of dsordere eating among athletes. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=-.53, p<.05";
  iadas:relationDirection "-";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "111";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

