  iadas:perspectives "Future longitudinal studies could determine the stability and the specificity of the ZOREAS, while an experimental study would help to etablish the direction of causality suggested by our correlation analysis. This type of research would help in developing educational programs based on self-regulation of eating attitude adaptation that seek to limit the emergence of dsordere eating among athletes. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "𝛃=-4.38, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "-";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "111";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Simple quadratic regression " .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1853> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "1853";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Performance approach goals were positive predictors of emerging disordered eating attitudes. Mastery avoidance goals were also positive predictors of disordered eating attitudes. Performance avoidance was a protective factor. A relationship between mastery approach and disturbed eating attitudes did not emerge in the structural equation model or the correlation table. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1853>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1853>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/figure%20skating>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/gymnastics>;
  iadas:limites "The data were self reported, suggesting the likelihood that social desirability was operative. The study was cross sectional, conclusions about causality cannot be inferred. The athletes scores on the eating psychopathology measure indicated relatively healthy attitudes, it is unclear whether the relationships observed would extend to athletes with more severe eating disorders. The generalization of the results is limited to the Female gender and an elite level. The participants ages and competition experience were not controlled. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """Future studies might investigate whether the relationships can be generalized to athletes in other types of sport or to other types of population, as well as the aforementioned variables that could play a moderation or mediation role in this relationship. Future studies could replicate with a sample of non-athletic controls, as well as a clinical sample in order to determine whether the mechanisms involved in the eating psychopathology of athletes are also operative in the general population and patients with eating disorders. The contextual and temporal dimensions could be considered, with future studies examining the current eating behavior, with a temporal control especially concerning the current goals. 
Programs could be adapted to encourage an orientation toward task mastery as a means to protect from disordered eating attitudes. """;
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.10, p=N.S.";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "196";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Aesthetic";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

