<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_1880> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "1880";
  iadas:authorConclusion "After accounting for indices of psychological wellbeing (self esteem, anxiety and depression), having supportive teammate frienships was the best predictor of lower eating psychopathology. Modelling of teammates disordered eating behaviours and perceived pressure from teammates to lose weight/change shape were the best predictors of higher disordered eating . Perceiving pressure from teammates to lose weight/change shape, in addition to perceiving that teammates engaged in disordered eating attitudes and behaviours were the strongest mechanisms of influence associated with elevated disordered eating and exercise behaviours. For Females, eating and exercise psychopathology were more strongly associated with indices of negative teammate influences than for males. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1880>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1880>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Aesthetic>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ball-game>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/endurance>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/power>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/team>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/technical>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/weight-class>;
  iadas:limites "Cross sectional design did not allow for cause and effect to be determined. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research should investigate whether susceptibility to teammate influences changes as a function of sport type and competitive level given research finding the athletes sport to be a key moderator in the development of disordered eating. Future research would benefit from assessing both teammate and coach influences in tandem to ascertain their relative strength when predicting disordered eating. Future research exclusively sampling athletes competing in team-based sports may indicate influences from teammates to have a greater impact on eating pathology. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.15, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "727";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

