  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_1975>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_1975>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Aesthetic>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ball-game>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/endurance>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/power>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/team>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/technical>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/weight-class>;
  iadas:limites "Although age and BMI were controlled for, it is acknowledged that there are a number of additional co-variates (e.g., perfectionism, athletic identity) that could have contributed to the findings of this study. The self report nature of the data collected and the context it was collected in (i.e., before/after a training session and in the company of teammates/coach) may potentially misrepresent athletes true behaviours. Items comprising the EDI-drive for thinness and body dissatsifaction subscales may not be an accurate reflection of male athletes experiences with disordered eating. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Identifying key risk factors and relevant moderators and mediators for eating psychopathology is important for effectively identifying those athletes at increased risk of eating and exercise psychopathology, and for developing appropriately tailored intervention and prevention strategies. Future research into the role of teammates would benefit from experimentally manipulating mechanisms of teammate influence on athletes actual food intake and should consider employing methodologies that are specifically tailored to male athletes. Employing modeeling analytic techniques to further our understanding of the complex, multi-factorial influences on athlete eating and exercise behaviours. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.11, N.S.";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "195";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Partial correlation" .

