<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "2";
  iadas:authorConclusion "This study highlights a positive association between exercise addiction and disordered eating, with body dysmorphic concerns and body appreciation acting as key mediating factors. It underscores the importance of psychological mechanisms in this relationship among young sport practitioners.";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Range%20of%20sports>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/including%20endurance>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/strength-based>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/team%20sports>;
  iadas:limites "The cross-sectional design prevents causal inferences, and the use of self-reported measures may introduce bias (e.g., social desirability, inaccurate reporting). Additionally, the specific sample limits the generalizability of the findings.";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future longitudinal and cross-cultural studies are needed to better understand these relationships and underlying mechanisms. Interventions targeting body image may help prevent disordered eating behaviors in this population.";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.67, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "321";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_20> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "20";
  iadas:authorConclusion "As muscle dysmorphia increases, orthorexia nervosa increases in individuals engaged in bodybuilding sports in the TRNC. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_20>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_20>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Bodybuilding>;
  iadas:limites "Since this study was conducted only on male bodybuilders, the findings cannot be generalized to Female bodybuilders.";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives """It is essential to provide education on muscle dysmorphia, orthorexia nervosa, and the use of ergogenic nutritional supplements in Physical Education and Sports Schools, as well as in coach training programs. Additionally, training on athlete nutrition and sports psychology in these institutions would equip them with knowledge about both athlete motivations and the mental health disorders frequently seen in athletes. Given the rise of these mental health issues in gyms, sports psychologists should be present in these environments, and mental health assessments should be conducted alongside medical evaluations for new memberships.
Conducting similar studies across different sports and with female participants could contribute valuable new insights to the literature.""";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.003, p=.96";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "200";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Aesthetic";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation " .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_200> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "200";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Body image has been found, not only to be a risk factor for the development of an ED, but as a mediator between perfectionism and dieting, and associated to performance cognitive anxiety which mediates the relationship between perfectionism and depression. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_200>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_200>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ballet>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/contemporary>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/flamenco>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/spanish%20folk>;
  iadas:limites "The use of general questionnaires such as the BDI II or EAT-26 which are not validated specifically to be used within the dance population, although they are validated and highly reliable measurements. Performance anxiety was measured hypothetically and it will be best to measure it previous to an event. Performance anxiety has been retrospectively measured instead of administering the questionnaires in situ before the performance. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives "Interventions aiming at reducing concern over mistakes may required a preventative component and by doing so it will help reducing body dissatisfaction, performance cognitive anxiety and dieting which will prevent the development of eating disorders in this vulnerable group. Future research should replicate this study and include males different age range, dance levels and nationalities. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.33, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "281";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Aesthetic";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation " .

