<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2027> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "2027";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Negative and positive aspects of the quality of the coach athlete and teammate athlete were related to athletes eating psychopathology after controlling for baseline eating psychopathology score. Conflict with the coach was found to be the only significant independent predictor of athletes eating psychopathology. The quality of the relationship with parents and attachmalet styles were not found to be related to athletes eating psychopathology 6 months later. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2027>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2027>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cycling>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/football>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/hockey>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/judo>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/rugby>;
  iadas:limites "The present findings are essentially correlational, thus preventing definitive conclusions about causality. The present study only examined the direct role of interpersonal relationships in atletes eating psychopathology. Fairburn et al. (2003) noted that interpersonal difficulties interact with other core psychopathological processes (low self esteem, clinical perfectionism, and mood intolerance) to potentially elicit and maintain eating disorders. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future studies should seek to examine how such processes as clinical perfectionism, self esteem, and mood intolerance interact with interpersonal difficulties to elicit eating psychopathology . And investigaite how these interpersonal variables interact with each other to predict athletes eating psychopathology. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.04, N.S.";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "122";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Partial correlation" .

