<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_204> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "204";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Body image has been found, not only to be a risk factor for the development of an ED, but as a mediator between perfectionism and dieting, and associated to performance cognitive anxiety which mediates the relationship between perfectionism and depression. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_204>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_204>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ballet>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/contemporary>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/flamenco>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/spanish%20folk>;
  iadas:limites "The use of general questionnaires such as the BDI II or EAT-26 which are not validated specifically to be used within the dance population, although they are validated and highly reliable measurements. Performance anxiety was measured hypothetically and it will be best to measure it previous to an event. Performance anxiety has been retrospectively measured instead of administering the questionnaires in situ before the performance. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives "Interventions aiming at reducing concern over mistakes may required a preventative component and by doing so it will help reducing body dissatisfaction, performance cognitive anxiety and dieting which will prevent the development of eating disorders in this vulnerable group. Future research should replicate this study and include males different age range, dance levels and nationalities. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.22, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "281";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Aesthetic";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation " .

