<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2083> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "2083";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Results indicated a moderate, positive and significant relationship between evaluative concerns and disordered eating. The associations of striving with the dimensions of eating psychopathology were both weak and one was non-significant. For each group, evaluative concerns was found to have a significant, positive association with the EAT and EDI-BD. Team/individuals athletes have significant positive associations between evaluative concerns and eating/body attitudes while aesthetic athletes had non-significant association between these variables. Regarding striving, team/indivdiual athletes maintained marginally-significant relationships between this dimension of perfectionism and the EAT, while aesthetic athletes maintained a non-significant association between the two variables. There is no relationship between striving and body dissatisfaction for team/indivdiual athletes. Aesthetic athletes displayed a significant negative association between striving and EDI-BD. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2083>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2083>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/basketball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cheerleading>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/crew>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cross%20country>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/diving>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/equestrian>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/field%20hockey>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ice%20hockey>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/lacrosse>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/rugby>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/skiing>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/soccer>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/squash>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/synchronized%20swimming>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/tennis>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/track%20and%20field>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ultimate%20frisbee>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>;
  iadas:limites "The data was collected exclusively at colleges with an NCAA Division III program. This lower level of competition may have affected the results. The sample size was small. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future studies may replicate the current methods aong a more competitive population as the degree of competitiveness enforced and internalized by athletes has been highlighted as an important predictor for the development of maladaptive psychological symptoms. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.295, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "478";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

