  iadas:authorConclusion "Professional players showed more positive body image, but a weak link between negative self-perception (especially strength) and ON risk was observed. Overall, ON is a relevant issue in soccer and requires attention from support staff.";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2110>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2110>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Soccer>;
  iadas:limites "The cross-sectional design and reliance on self-reported data limit causal conclusions, and the inclusion of only male players restricts generalizability";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research should include longitudinal designs and more diverse samples (e.g., female athletes) to better understand risk factors and develop targeted prevention and support programs";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.204, NS";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "137";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Team sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Ball game";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

