<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2119> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "2119";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Self-oriented perfectionism, through obsessive passion was related to higher levels of disordered eating. We did not find mediating effects for obsessive passion in the relationship between socially prescribed perfectionism and disordered eating, and for harmonious passion in the relationship between self oriented perfectionism and physical well-being or disordered eating. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2119>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2119>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/artistic%20swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/gymnastics>;
  iadas:limites "Self reported measures. Recruitment of participants via MTurk may limit the generalizability of the representativeness. Although study 2 used a longitudinal design, there were only two timepoints and the sample size was relatively small. The instrument used was not intended to diagnose eating disorders. Important markers of eating psychopathology were not used. We included both recreational and competitive athletes. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """Further research is deemed necessary to replicate the results of
this research and further extend our understanding of the psychological
processes involved in disordered eating and physical and psychological
well-being in a broader set of sports and participants.""";
  iadas:relationDegree " r=.16, N.S.";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "107";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Aesthetic";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_212> iadas:analysisId "212";
  iadas:authorConclusion "This study shows that disordered eating is significantly associated with lower HRQOL in adolescent athletes, even at subclinical levels, particularly affecting psychosocial functioning. Female athletes appear more vulnerable to reduced HRQOL.";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_212>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_212>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Football>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Soccer>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/baseball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/basketball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cross%20country>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/dance>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/diving>;
  a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ice%20hockey>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/lacrosse>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/softball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/tennis>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/track%20and%20field>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>;
  iadas:limites "Methodological challenges in measuring energy availability, reliance on self-reported data, and limited generalizability (single region, sport dominance, no control group) may affect the findings.";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future studies should explore mediating factors and better assess energy availability and symptoms. Early screening and targeted interventions are essential to improve HRQOL in young athletes.";
