    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Figure%20skating%20%28synchronized%29>;
  iadas:limites "Smaller sample. Weight pressures may be experienced differently according to discipline specific performance demands. Cross sectional design. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives """Future research should incorporate longitudinal designs to identify true risk factors of ED symptomatology and use qualitative interviews to further examine the lived experience of sport-related weight pressures. 
Practitioners may collaborate with other professionals, such as sports dieteticians, to educate skating communities on weight-performance myths and improve communication between skaters, parents, and coaches about the body. Practitioners may also assist athletes in coping with weight pressures by focusing on body appreciation and function while reinforcing that healthy training approaches can have positive effects on eating, exercise, and body image. """;
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.58, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "29";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Aesthetic";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Intercorrelation" .

