<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2324> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "2324";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Although pthological orthorexic eating and exercise addiction may co-occur and correlate moderately, their link can neither be explained by restriction in well-being nor participation in specific sports categories. A non-pathological interest in healthyeating may slightly enhance well-being in men, but orthorexia nervosa may be detrimental to women's well-being only. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2324>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2324>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Endurance>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/aesthetical>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/antigravitation>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/fitness>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/health>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/martial%20arts>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/rehabilitation>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/resistance>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/team>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/technical>;
  iadas:limites "Reliance on self-reported exercise activity and conveniance sampling may have introduced biases, such as self-selection and social desirability, which limit the validity of our results. Recruitment tool place in different locations, we cannot completely exclude overlap of participants across samples. The unequal gender distribution and small sample size who practiced martial arts and rehabilitation sports constrain generalizability. Without measuring disordered eating, we could not differentiate betweenn instrumental exercise aimed at improvng appearance and exercise addiction. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Prevention and treatment strategies for excessive health behaviors should focus on helping women maintain a balanced approach to healthy eating and assisting men in regulating their exercise activities. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=-.269, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "-";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "1064";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

