<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2345> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "2345";
  iadas:authorConclusion "This study demonstrating the detrimental effects of psychological abuse on athletes, specifically with respect to the increased risk of eating disorder and self-harm indicators. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2345>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2345>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/athletics>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cycling>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/freestyle%20skiing>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/gymnastics>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/rowing>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/rugby>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>;
  iadas:limites "The current methods were limited by the use of non-validated questionnaires, subsets of validated scales, and the use of a narrow population of athletes. Findings did not differentiate between maltreatment perpetrated by coaches, teammates, parents or other perpetrators? ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Recommendations include increasing education for coaches and other sport participants, particularly on the scope of what behaviors constitute psychological abuse and the potentially harmful impacts of these behaviors on athletes. Increased awareness of the dangers of promoting adherence to the sport ethic, which emphasizes a culture that promotes self-sacrifice and accepting excessive demands, is also necessary given the potential negative impacts on athlete mental health.";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.311, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "794";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

