<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_237> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "237";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Goal orientation, body dissatisfaction, and negative behavior and pressure from coaches significantly contribute to the risk of ED development in female and male cadet, junior and non-elite athletes, while body dissatisfaction seems to be the strongest predictor, especially in female athletes. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_237>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_237>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Taekwondo>;
  iadas:limites "The sample size, although it is realistic in relation to the number of active taekwondo competitors in Croatia. Self reported questionnaires. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives "Including other measures, more adjusted to male ED symptoms. As the results showed the significance of the behavior of coaches in relation to athletes ED symptoms, it would be very interesting to investigate the transgenerational transfer of distorted values, beliefs and behaviors related to ED from coaches to athletes, i.e., to investigate coaches history of ED symptoms and their current behavior. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.14, N.S.";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "132 (male)";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Weight sensitive";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Spearman correlation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_2372> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "2372";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Weight-sensitive sports and higher levels of shame and guilt were associated with greater eating pathology symptoms (EPS), while non-weight-sensitive sports may have a protective effect. The findings highlight the role of both sport environment and moral emotions in understanding disordered eating in athletes";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_2372>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_2372>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Weight%20sensitive%20sport>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/non-weight%20sensitive%20sport>;
  iadas:limites "The study relied on self-reported data and a nonclinical, relatively homogeneous sample, limiting generalizability and introducing potential biases. Additionally, modest effect sizes and the cross-sectional design restrict causal interpretations";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research should use longitudinal and mixed-method approaches to examine additional factors like perfectionism and coaching pressure. This could improve early detection and inform targeted prevention strategies in athletic settings";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.287, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "130";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

