<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_478> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "478";
  iadas:authorConclusion "The coach athlete relationship may be a critical and controllable mediating factor in the development of DE in Female collegiate athletes, especially in endurance sports. The coach athlete relationship did not predict DE for aesthetic athletes. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_478>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_478>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/basketball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cross%20country>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/dance>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/diving>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/drill%20team>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/lacrosse>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/soccer>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/softball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/track%20and%20field>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>;
  iadas:limites "A limitation of the study is the use of self-report data which introduces self-report bias. Moreover, because this study was nonexperimental, it was possible to control for contributing and confounding variables. Moreover, given the cross-sectional design of the study, causality could not be determined. Although structural equation modeling is more forgiving with this limitation that other methods, allowing the research to measure influence, causality remains elusive. Although, team was hypothesized to a nesting variable, it was not significant. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """Further research is necessary to fully understand the role of the coach-athlete relationship on weight-related coach pressyre and disordered eating behaviors in a wide range of contexts. Due to limitations in the data, future research should test the mediational model representing the coach-athlete relationship with equal numbers of athletes in each sport type for each category of a nesting variables, such as chool or sport. Threfore, if education of the role of the coach on disordered eating behaviorrs can be incorporated into coaching education programs, the effectiveness of such interventions should be measured in future studies. 
The relationship between past coach comments to lose weight or maintain a low body weight and current weight-related coach pressure suggests that coaches should be educated about the potential short and long term effects of weight related comments. Therefore, coaches should be aware of their influence in the eating behaviors of their athletes. If possible, coaches should strive to minimize the perception of weight-related coach pressure and strengthen their relationships with their athletes. These implications may be especially important for coaches of endurance athletes who most reflected this model whereas aesthetic coaches should likely focus their efforts more on the communication of weight-related coach pressure. """;
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.30, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "244";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

