<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_540> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "540";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Only the sociocultural factors and body fat dissatisfaction adhered to etiological model of DE in Brazilian male athletes. Sociocultural factors (parents, friends and the media) exhibit a direct relationship to DE. The results of the structural equation model indicate that body fat dissatisfaction mediates the relationship between sociocultural factors and DE.";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_540>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_540>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/basketball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/boxing>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/canoeing>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cycling>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/diving>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/equestrian>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/jiu-jitsu>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/judo>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/rowing>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/sailing>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/surfing>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/swimming>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/tae-kwon-do>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/tennis>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/track%20and%20field>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/triathlon>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/water%20polo>;
  iadas:limites "Because self-reporting instruments were used as evaluative tools, the results may not reflect the reality because the responses given were subjective. The study is also limited in that it applies a doubly indirect method to evaluate fat percentages. Weight and body fat measurements can influence the survey responses about body image and disordered eating. The heterogeneity of the sample with respect to age and type of sport could have influenced the results. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Sport professionals may use the present study findings to intervene in factors that promote disturbed eating in athletes. Because disordered eating can cause an attenuation of anaerobic potency and resistance, prevention/intervention programs that are designed to prevent disordered eating in athletes may indirectly improve athletic performance. The construction of a socio-sports model for Female is recommaleded. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.28, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "321";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

