    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/football>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/handball>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/jiu-jitsu>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/judo>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/olympic%20weightlifting>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/ornamental%20jumping>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/rowing>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/sailing>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/swimming>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/tae-kwon-do>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/tennis>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/triathlon>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/water%20polo>;
  iadas:limites "Since we used self-reported instruments as assessment tools, the result may not reflect th context analyzed, because the responses were subjective. Portuguese is the langage spoken in Brazil and Portugal, but these countries have significant cultural differences and also small changes in their own writing. In this sense, the use of such a psychometric instrument in this study may have influenced the results obtained. Another limitation is that we used only the total score of the instruments, maling impossible the mediating role of ACSI-28 subscales in the association between anxiety and eating disorders. In addition, this study was restricted to the evaluation of psychological variables of athletes in just one moment, which does not characterize the real relationships of cause and effect between the variables. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """Future investigations should use a prospective approach with the athletes, besides crossing the previously described psychological variables with the performance levels during the season. 
We suggest further investigations with male Brazilian athletes to confirm the findings of this study. Furthermore, it is recommaleded the construction of an etiological model of eating disorder for Brazilian athletes of both sexes. The practical results of this study are in the possibility of sports professionals, more specifically, sports psychologists, to develop interventions that make it possible to decrease the level of competitive anxiety and/or enhance the development of coping strategies to reduce the triggering of eating disorders in Brazilian male athletes. """;
  iadas:relationDegree "r=-.45, p<.05";
  iadas:relationDirection "-";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "739";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Intercorrelation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_555> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "555";
  iadas:authorConclusion "There was a significantly positive relationship between muscle dysmorphia disorder inventory and eating attitude test in both professional and recreational bodybuilders. There is a significant positive correlation between body dissatisfaction and eating disorders in bodybuilders. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_555>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_555>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Bodybuilding>;
  iadas:limites "One limitation of this study is its inability to speculate causality. Although this study demonstrated significant correlation of eating disorders and body dissatisfaction, the study was not able to determine whether such a trend can be generalized to athletes of all sexes. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives "In this study, it was identified that the combined use of three screening tools could provide useful information to health care professionals for early detection of eating and body image-related problems in male bodybuilders";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.614, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "120";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Aesthetic";
