<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_611> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "611";
  iadas:authorConclusion "The mediation analysis suggests that inadequate relational styles with parents can invaludate the emotional regulation of adolescents and encourage orthorexia behaviours. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_611>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_611>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Volleyball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/basket>;
  iadas:limites "First, the use of self-report questionnaires could provide information that is not pure because answers might be affected by social desirability. Another limitation is the cross-sectional nature of the current study. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """Coach and practicioners could incorporate aspects of emotional regulation interventions into practices or as supplemental activities to the season. For example, the coach could incorporate lunches with a sport psychologist, who could discuss emotional regulation tactics with the athletes. Similarly, the coach could incorporate goal-setting activities throughout the season, with a focus on how to set smart goals, and then how to regulate emotions through the challenges of achieving such goals. 
Future research could verify this model in a multi-time perspective as well as including personality and social variables that can be configured as risk and/or protective factors for the etiology of orthorexia. Finally, a longitudinal persceptive would enable a better exploration, through adolescent development, of the indivdiual differences in terms of both emotional and family variables, mainly in adolescents at risk of compulsive behaviours. """;
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.23, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "303";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Team sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Ball game";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_612> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "612";
  iadas:authorConclusion "The mediation analysis suggests that inadequate relational styles with parents can invaludate the emotional regulation of adolescents and encourage orthorexia behaviours. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_612>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_612>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Volleyball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/basket>;
  iadas:limites "First, the use of self-report questionnaires could provide information that is not pure because answers might be affected by social desirability. Another limitation is the cross-sectional nature of the current study. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """Coach and practicioners could incorporate aspects of emotional regulation interventions into practices or as supplemental activities to the season. For example, the coach could incorporate lunches with a sport psychologist, who could discuss emotional regulation tactics with the athletes. Similarly, the coach could incorporate goal-setting activities throughout the season, with a focus on how to set smart goals, and then how to regulate emotions through the challenges of achieving such goals. 
Future research could verify this model in a multi-time perspective as well as including personality and social variables that can be configured as risk and/or protective factors for the etiology of orthorexia. Finally, a longitudinal persceptive would enable a better exploration, through adolescent development, of the indivdiual differences in terms of both emotional and family variables, mainly in adolescents at risk of compulsive behaviours. """;
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.20, p<.001";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "303";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Team sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Ball game";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

