<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_7> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "7";
  iadas:authorConclusion "This study supports a dual-pathway model of muscle dysmorphia, where sociocultural pressure influences symptoms both indirectly via appearance motivation and directly, with cognitive flexibility acting as a protective moderator. It highlights the interplay between social, motivational, and cognitive factors";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_7>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_7>;
  iadas:limites "The cross-sectional design limits causal interpretation, and the use of a convenience, all-male sample restricts generalizability. Additionally, the measure of sociocultural pressure was not specific to muscularity ideals";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research should use longitudinal designs and more diverse samples to validate the model. Interventions enhancing cognitive flexibility and promoting non-appearance-based exercise motives appear promising avenues for prevention and treatment.";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=-.228, p<.05";
  iadas:relationDirection "-";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "95";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_70> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "70";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Protective and facilitative role of self-compassion in body appreciation, intuitive eating, disordered eating, compulsive exercise, and self-criticism for Canadian Female athletes";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_70>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_70>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cheerleading>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/dance>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/track%20and%20field>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>;
  iadas:limites "An updated version of the BAS was published after all study data had been collected.";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """(a) Explore Female athletes’ self-compassion, body and eating attitudes and behaviors overtime and within specific sport and international cultural contexts.
(b) it is unclear how body appreciation and intuitive eating are related to sport performance.""";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.42, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "90";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Pearson correlation " .

<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_709> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "709";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Self determined motivation was negatively associated with external ingestion, emotional ingestion, and constraint. In constrast, non self determined motivation was associated with external ingestion, emotional ingestion, and constraint. Individuals who engage in more physical activity have a more self-determined regulation of their eating habits, whereas those who engage in less physical activity have a less determined regulation of their eating habits. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_709>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_709>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/cross%20training>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/weightlifting>;
  iadas:limites "The fact that the data were self-reported and collected online is a clear limitation. In addition, due to the sample's characteritics, we were unable to explore possible differences across age groups and sex. The International Physical Activity Questionnaire shirt version is a validated and simple method for estimating physical activity levels. However, it is not an objecive assessment and only considers a limited period (only 7 days). Furthermore, only the MET was assessed, with no cinsideration given to other characteristics such as sedentary behaviors. This study is a cross-sectional, which is also a limitation due to the fact that individuals were evaluated in a single moment, which may not fully reflect their eating behaviors. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives "We suggest that future studies explore possible moderation variables (age, sex, gym facility and exercise activity) that could influence the current results. It is worth emphasizing the scarcity of longitudinal and experimental research that investigates how interventions grounded in self determination theory could enhance physical activity as a mean to increase healthy eating habits. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=-.69, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "-";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "440";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Individual sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

