<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_721> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "721";
  iadas:authorConclusion "Socially prescribed perfectionism did not explain variance in dietary restraint scores. Self esteem oriented perfectionism was associated with dietary restraint and was related to body dissatisfaction. The current findings show a mediating effect of body esteem weight satisfaction on the relationship between self-oriented perfectionism and dietary restraint. The perfectionist personality would be a contributing factor in dietary restraint required to maintin a low body weight. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_721>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_721>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Synchronized%20swimming>;
  iadas:limites "Limitations of the study were linked to self-report measures and the cross-sectional nature of the investigations. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "One";
  iadas:perspectives "Future research is needed to gain a fuller understanding of the relationship between these three variable. The use of both self-report measures and interview formats in longitudinal studies must be developed to gain a more precise estimate of the nature and extent of inappropriate compensatory behaviours amog synchronized swimmers. ";
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.49, p<.01";
  iadas:relationDirection "+";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "33";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Team sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Aesthetic";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Correlation" .

