<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Analysis_927> a iadas:Analysis;
  iadas:analysisId "927";
  iadas:authorConclusion "SPA scores contributed to dieting and bulimia scores in individual athletes. SPA and sport type independently and in combination contribute to greater dieting and bulimic behavior, particularly in Female individual sport athletes. ";
  iadas:complexityOfAnalysis "Simple analyses";
  iadas:groupStatisticalAnalysis "Correlation";
  iadas:hasPopulation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Population_927>;
  iadas:hasRelation <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/data/Relations_927>;
  iadas:hasSport <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Netball>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/aerobics>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/diving>, <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/soccer>,
    <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/volleyball>;
  iadas:limites "Only athletes attending the training would have been approached about the study. Not all athletes from each sport at each institute were present at the time of data collection due to other commutmalets. Most athletes were tested at training sessions, rather than in settings which might heighten SPA. The testing of athletes in this manner may identify more consistent levels of SPA and disordered eating. This division by team and individual sport may be too simplisticc, not accounting for other psychological and confounding factors. These factors may affect disordered eating. ";
  iadas:numberOfSportStudied "Multiple";
  iadas:perspectives """Longitudinal and experimental designs may elucidate the directionality of the relationship, providing support for possible interventions. 
Female indivdiual sport athletes in particular may benefit from practical methods of reducing SPA and encouraging healthy eating within the sport setting by coaches and peers. 
Attention to other trigger factors may be necessary when dealing with Female athletes in individual sports, as this subgroup reported the highest levels of dieting and bulimic tendencies, along with high SPA. Different techniques and strategies for dealing with SPA and disordered eating may be required for different sport types. """;
  iadas:relationDegree "r=.10, p=N.S.";
  iadas:relationDirection "NS";
  iadas:sampleSizeMobilized "84 (team sport)";
  iadas:sportPracticeType "Mixed sport";
  iadas:sportSubcategory "Multisport ";
  iadas:typeOfAnalysis "Bivariate correlation" .

